Z||000002||Jaygee79||03-09-2001||11:31 AM||||You know, maybe if more kids were taught how to use guns properly and to respect them instead of them just being 'off limits', maybe there wouldn't be so much of a problem.  My grandfather taught me how to shoot when I was 8 years old.  I grew up knowing how to use them, but also knowing how much damage they can cause and to respect them.  If you go up to Maine you see 12 year-old kids walking down the street carrying rifles, but you never hear of any problems up there.  That's because they are taught right from the start not to be afraid to touch them, but how to handle them properly.<p>[This message has been edited by Jaygee79 (edited 03-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||03-09-2001||11:39 AM||||Agreed.  That's how I was raised too.<BR>(There was a REAL long thread on this topic last year)||||reg||6
