Z||000005||loafer87gt||03-09-2001||12:17 PM||||I was just reading through the paper and it sounds like the police very very lucky. I guess the guy called a cab to go to the univesity, but when he got there, he didn't want to go in, and refused to pay the cabbie. I guess the cabbie noticed that he was concealing a shotgun and called it in to the police, who came and apprehended him.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||beer_stud_21||03-09-2001||04:20 PM||||I think the gun respect thing has a lot of merit.  So does the good parenting.  I just turned 20, and was given my first gun when I was 5.  It was a .22cal pellet pistol handed down to me by my dad.  He had it when he was a boy and he taught me how to use it.  I'm also mild mannered and have been raised in a 5 person family with 2 (married) parents.  But on the other hand all growing up I was teased for being tall, skinny, big ears, lazy eye, funny name.. etc etc.. Did i kill anybody..?  NO.. Even though I would fit the description of one of these school shooters.  Can i explain why? Personally I can't figure out how these kids think to do something like this in the first place..  I had the oppertunity and motive for something like this many times when i was in school, but its just not something an emotionally stable person thinks about IMHO. I think its a mixture of a lot of things.  1 part personality, 2 parts family life, 1 part disipline.  I think the sepereated parents, 2 working parents, kids that feed themselves out of the microwave during commercials has something to do with it.  (wether they are watching violent TV shows or not.  But then again I didnt have a TV until i was about 10yrs old.  Maybe seeing this stuff when your so young has an effect, just like how some little kids can't tell when the computer generated special effects in movies are real or not.)  What do you guys think?<P>-Marlynn.. now spelled "Marlin" so it doesnt confuse poeple. ||||reg||1
